<newsitem itemid="405227" id="root" date="1997-02-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Prudential profits inflated by disposal gain.</title>
<headline>Prudential profits inflated by disposal gain.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31 1996</p>
<p>				   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		73.4		   vs 39.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 11.5		   vs 10.4</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 17.3		   vs 15.7</p>
<p> Total gross premiums   11.579 bln	   vs 8.519 bln</p>
<p> Pretax post-except     1.614 bln	    vs 1.044 bln</p>
<p> Operating profit	 873		    vs 804</p>
<p>NOTE - The pretax profit figure and the earnings per share reflect a 797 million stg profit from disposals versus a 31 million gain in 1995. The operating result shows underlying growth which is above the average analyst forecast.</p>
<p>Full company name -- Prudential Corp Plc</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
</text>
